WEBVTT

NOTE LUMO, The Gospel of Luke 14:1-15:10 (Arclight 6_GOLuke2615), en.
NOTE Timings: whisper.cpp small -dtw small per speech burst on the isolated dialogue (dialoguenhance centre channel), first word on the burst start, 2026-11-20.

1
00:00:54.550 --> 00:00:58.350
When he noticed how the guests picked the places of honor at the table,

2
00:00:58.900 --> 00:01:00.350
he told them this parable:

3
00:01:01.700 --> 00:01:04.200
When someone invites you to a wedding feast,

4
00:01:04.750 --> 00:01:06.550
do not take the place of honor,

5
00:01:06.650 --> 00:01:10.050
for a person more distinguished than you may have been invited.

6
00:01:10.150 --> 00:01:14.550
If so, the host who invited both of you will come and say to you,

7
00:01:14.950 --> 00:01:16.990
Give this person your seat.

8
00:01:17.090 --> 00:01:22.520
Then, humiliated, you will have to take the least important place.

9
00:01:22.620 --> 00:01:25.700
But when you are invited, take the lowest place,

10
00:01:26.250 --> 00:01:28.520
so that when your host comes, he will say to you,

11
00:01:28.620 --> 00:01:32.530
Friend, move up to a better place.

12
00:01:32.630 --> 00:01:36.950
Then you will be honored in the presence of all the other guests.

13
00:01:37.600 --> 00:01:41.080
For all those who exalt themselves will be humbled,

14
00:01:41.180 --> 00:01:44.550
and those who humble themselves will be exalted.
